// S441 reproducer — addendum-2 S3a: the §55.1 `is some` validator on a cell declaration silently drops the cell.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/site-is-some-cell-validator-drops-decl.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: §55.1 universal-core table row: `is some` | "Value exists …" | example use `<x is some>` |
//           error tag `.NotSome`. The cell is declared with a validity surface.
// Actual:   exit 1, but the declaration itself draws NO diagnostic; the cell is never registered, so the
//           later reads fail: `E-SCOPE-001: Unquoted identifier `@mid` in attribute `bind:value`…` and
//           `E-STATE-UNDECLARED: bare `@mid` read with no reactive cell in scope…` — both blame the read
//           sites. Same with a type: `<mid: string is some> = ""`. Other validators (`req`, `gt(0)`) parse.
<program>
<mid is some> = ""
<input bind:value=@mid>
<p>${@mid}</p>
</program>
